TEXT 0 -416 Left 2 ;Problem 4.4a - Problem 4.2 in LTspice: baffled piston (S = 100 cm^2, 20 g), 2 cm thick baffle (tube d), 40 L box on the back
TEXT 0 -384 Left 2 ;TOP: mechanical IMPEDANCE analogy (force = voltage, velocity = current).   BOTTOM: mechanical MOBILITY analogy (velocity = voltage, force = current)
TEXT 0 -336 Left 2 !.param rho=1.2 c=343 S=0.01 Mmp=0.02 V=0.04 d=0.02 a={sqrt(S/pi)}
TEXT 0 -304 Left 2 !.param Ma={rho*d/S} Ca={V/(rho*c**2)} Ma1={8*rho/(3*pi**2*a)} Ra1={0.441*rho*c/S} Ra2={rho*c/S} Ca1={5.94*a**3/(rho*c**2)}
TEXT 0 -112 Left 2 ;impedance analogy
TEXT 0 720 Left 2 ;mobility analogy
TEXT 0 1408 Left 2 !.ac dec 10000 1 20k
TEXT 0 1456 Left 2 ;a) f/u: 1 m/s drives the top circuit, so V(f) = Z_M;  1 N drives the bottom one, so 1/V(u_m) = Z_M.  The two curves must lie on top of each other.
TEXT 0 1488 Left 2 ;Z_M = j w Mmp + S^2 [Z_ar + j w (Ma + Ma1) + 1/(j w Ca)]:  sharp minimum at 20.4 Hz (official: 20.4 Hz), then mass line.  I(Vu) = u, V(pf)-V(pb) = p
